  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On a playlist with (for example) 3 files, if you have a dynamic URL of some kind (via an external redirection script), the videoplayer will only see the first result. As in:\n\n1. Queue 3 videos.\n2. Watch all 3.\n3. Before the third ends (and the player proceeds back to the first), change the redirection URL in your script/whatever to a new source.\n4. The player will not play the redirected URL. It will instead play the original video file, apparently cached.\n\nThe VideoSync player should check to see if the resolved URL of a playlist item has changed since its last play, and if it has changed, download the new file and play it.\n\nMaking this change will allow for much more robust VideoSync player use, as it would allow for external playlists, randomization, etc.",
